x32dbg / x64dbg Malware Analysis Breakpoint Reference
A classroom-oriented reference for Windows 10 x86/x64 dynamic analysis in an isolated FLARE-VM. Covers DLL/process injection, hollowing, thread activity, file writes, memory, anti-analysis, persistence, and network activity.
Usage: The comma-separated bp lines are reference lists, not executable x32dbg commands. To set a group, paste one bp command per line into the x32dbg Script tab, or enter each command individually. Resolve exports against the actual loaded module (for example kernel32, kernelbase, ntdll, advapi32, ws2_32, wininet, winhttp, or dnsapi). Some functions are forwarded, absent, or inlined on particular builds. Avoid enabling every breakpoint simultaneously.

