Beyond API breakpoints: In x86, malware may inspect the PEB through FS:[30h] and the BeingDebugged byte at PEB offset 0x02 without calling an API. Inspect disassembly and cross-references; an API breakpoint will not catch that direct read. NtQueryInformationProcess classes commonly associated with debugger checks include ProcessDebugPort (7), ProcessDebugObjectHandle (0x1E), and ProcessDebugFlags (0x1F).

